        "can_recover": false,
        "can_see_hidden_post": false,
        "can_wiki": false,
        "read": false,
        "user_title": "Chief Justice",
        "title_is_group": false,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "For reference:\n\n[quote=\"\"Focused Apertures\"\"]\nIncrease cold damage dealt by Absolute Zero by 1.\n[/quote]\n\n\n[quote=\"\"Modular Realignment\"\"]\nSelect 1 Equipment card from your Trash and put it either into your hand or into play. Absolute Zero deals himself 1 fire damage and 1 cold damage.\n[/quote]\n\n\n[quote=\"\"Null-Point Calibration Unit\"\"]\nWhen Absolute Zero would take cold damage, regain that many HP instead.\n[/quote]\n\n\nSo, in the example cited above, the following events would happen in the following order:\n\n[list type=decimal]\n[*]The player would remove Null-Point Calibration Unit from their Trash and put it into play.\n[*]Modular Realignment would deal Absolute Zero 1 fire damage.\n[*]Modular Realignment would deal Absolute Zero 1 cold damage, which would actually be 2 cold damage because of Focused Apertures.  Because Modular Realignment is in play, Absolute Zero would regain 2 HP instead of losing 2 HP\n[/list]\n\nThe sequence of events gets even more complex if Isothermic Transducer is in play.  In that case:\n\n[list type=decimal]\n[*]The player would remove Null-Point Calibration Unit from their Trash and put it into play.\n[*]Modular Realignment would deal Absolute Zero 1 fire damage.\n[*]Absolute Zero could then deal the target of his choice 1 cold damage, which would actually be 2 cold damage because of Focused Apertures.\n[*]Modular Realignment would deal Absolute Zero 1 cold damage, which would actually be 2 cold damage because of Focused Apertures.  Because Modular Realignment is in play, Absolute Zero would regain 2 HP instead of losing 2 HP\n[/list]\n\nCryochamber makes this sequence of events *even more* thrilling... and that's why I love Absolute Zero :)",
