        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "[quote=\"\"Paul\"\"]\n\nCryochamber makes this sequence of events *even more* thrilling... and that's why I love Absolute Zero :)\n\n[/quote]\n\n\nLet me see if I can work this out. Imagine that Legacy has used his Galvanize power and Absolute Zero has Focused Aperture, Isothermic Transducer, and Cryo Chamber, then uses Modular Realignment to get the Null-point Calibration Unit and put it in to play:\n\n[list type=decimal]\n[*]The Modular Realignment deals Absolute Zero 1 Fire Damage, which is decreased by one due to the Cryo Chamber, but increased by one due to Legacy's Galvanize. Absolute Zero takes one point of fire damage\n[*] Due to the Isothermic Transducer, Absolute Zero may then deal one target one cold damage, which is increased by one due to Focused Apertures and increased by another one due to Legacy's Galvanize, so Absolute Zero may deal one target three cold damage.\n[*] The Modular Realignment then deals Absolute Zero 1 Cold Damage, which is increased by one due to the Cryo Chamber, increased by one due to the Focused Aperture, increased by one due to Legacy's Galvanize, and turned into healing by the Null-Point Calibration Unit, so Absolute Zero regains up to four hit points.\n[/list]\n\nI'm pretty sure that's right -- just using this post as a way to work through it all.",
